   "evidence": "Presheaf/Stalk.lean:112-125 (`@[expose] def germSemilinear` with \"It is exposed so that it agrees with `germ` by `rfl` downstream\", followed by `@[simp] theorem germSemilinear_apply \u2026 := rfl`); Presheaf/TensorProduct/Stalk.lean:63-68 (`tensorGermMap_tmul \u2026 := by rfl`) and 106-117 (term proof whose RHS differs from `stalkLiftCommRing_germ`'s `f U hx m` only by that unfolding); `TensorProduct.map_tmul` for semilinear maps exists at mathlib/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/TensorProduct/Map.lean:59.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Presheaf/Stalk.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `@[expose]` and the sentence justifying it from the docstring. Prove `tensorGermMap_tmul` from `TensorProduct.map_tmul` plus `germSemilinear_apply` (the `eqToHom` cast is private and in-file, so a `show`/`erw` handles it), and chain `tensorStalkComparison_germ_tmul` as `(\u2026 stalkLiftCommRing_germ \u2026).trans (tensorGermMap_tmul \u2026)` instead of relying on defeq.",
   "issue": "`@[expose] def germSemilinear` exposes the body only to let downstream files reduce it to `germ` by `rfl` (its docstring says so), although the `@[simp]` lemma `germSemilinear_apply` (line 123) is exactly that interface. The two consumers rely on the defeq: `tensorGermMap_tmul` is `by rfl` and the term proof of `tensorStalkComparison_germ_tmul` only typechecks by unfolding `germSemilinear` (Presheaf/TensorProduct/Stalk.lean:68, :116). This locks the implementation into the public API and is against the repo's stated practice (TauCeti/Algebra/TensorProduct/BaseChange.lean:45 \"their bodies are not `@[expose]`d, and the `_tmul` ... lemmas are the interface\"; Algebra/Quaternion/ComplexSubfield.lean:76 on using `(rfl)`).",
   "line": "115"
  }
 ],
